# Architecture & Runtime

- **Monorepo:** `frontend/` (SvelteKit) + `backend/` (Go Fiber). Atomic commits; separate execution.
- **Production / local run:** Only the Go binary serves the app. **Never** `npm run dev` or `npm start` as the runtime entrypoint.
- **Build:** `npm run build` → static assets → `go:embed` in `backend/ui/static` → `go build`. See `docs/development.md`.

```
TTRPG-Toolkit/
├── frontend/src/lib/   # components, stores, utils, api, types
├── frontend/src/routes/
├── backend/cmd/        # main
├── backend/internal/   # api, server, config, (services, repository, ws as added)
├── backend/ui/static/  # embed target (generated)
├── build/static/       # SvelteKit adapter output (generated)
├── docs/
└── .env                # backend config (from .env.example); not config.yaml
```

- **HTTP:** Fiber serves embedded SPA on `/`, API on `/api/*`. Frontend config only via `GET /api/config`.
- **Docker:** Multi-stage Dockerfile (Node build → Go embed + compile → minimal runtime). Caddy proxies in Compose.

## Fast local iteration (dev only)

| Change | Command |
|--------|---------|
| UI only (ship parity) | `go generate ./backend/ui/...` then `go build -C backend -o ttrpg-toolkit ./cmd` |
| Go/API only | `go build -C backend -o ttrpg-toolkit ./cmd` |
| UI preview (HMR) | Go binary on `:8080` + `npm run dev` in `frontend/` (proxies `/api`; not production) |

Skip `npm ci` unless `package-lock.json` changed.

## Dependencies

No new NPM/Go package for logic writable cleanly in &lt;20 lines of stdlib. Conventional Commits: `feat(scope): subject`.
